[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124771,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Naevus spilus is a benign melanocytic naevus presenting as a hyperpigmented patch containing a variable number of darker macules or papules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124772,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8720/0 Naevus spilus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124773,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F20.Y &amp; XH40S8 Other specific types of melanocytic naevus &amp; Naevus spilus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124774,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> speckled lentiginous naevus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124775,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124776,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Naevus spilus can occur at any anatomical site. In rare cases it can be seen in the oral cavity {28045755}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124777,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Naevus spilus appears as a light-brown patch with black, brown, or reddish-brown macules or papules within it. It is usually 30&ndash;60&nbsp;mm in diameter, and the speckles within it are commonly 2&ndash;3&nbsp;mm in size. Approximately 80% of these lesions are present at birth or appear during early infancy. They may initially present as caf&eacute;-au-lait macules, with the hyperpigmented macules and papules developing later {11176689}.</p>\r\n<p>In phakomatosis pigmentokeratotica (concomitant naevus sebaceus and naevus spilus), patients additionally have a separate orange-yellow pebbly plaque representing the naevus sebaceus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124778,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prevalence of naevus spilus (0.2&ndash;2.8% depending on age) is similar to that of congenital melanocytic naevi {4004301; 17241580; 2187718}. There is no ethnic or sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124779,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "<p>Genetic and environmental factors may play a role in the occurrence of naevus spilus.</p>\r\n<h5>Genetic susceptibility</h5>\r\n<p>Speckled lentiginous naevus syndrome has been characterized as a distinct neurocutaneous phenotype in which ipsilateral neurological abnormalities are present in association with naevus spilus {11872407; 19706091; 15459538}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124780,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Naevi spilus probably represent clonal populations of melanocytes resulting from a postzygotic <em>HRAS</em> mutation in a melanocyte precursor. The mutation is present in the background macule, with the individual darker papules having additional alterations, including amplification of the mutant <em>HRAS</em> allele {24751729; 24390138}. Mosaic translocations have been demonstrated in agminated Spitz naevi within a naevus spilus {32004563; 32386465}. Phakomatosis pigmentokeratotica may harbour <em>HRAS</em> or <em>KRAS</em> mutations {28523882}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124781,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124782,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>The background hyperpigmented patch has elongated, hyperpigmented rete ridges with slightly increased numbers of melanocytes. The speckles show variable findings, including those of lentiginous junctional, compound or intradermal, congenital-pattern, Spitz, or blue naevi, and naevi with cytological atypia {32386465}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes caf&eacute;-au-lait macules, agminated melanocytic naevi, and partial unilateral lentiginosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:30:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124783,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124784,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124785,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a hyperpigmented patch containing multiple small darker papules or macules.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> patch area showing a mild increase in small junctional melanocytes and darker areas showing benign junctional or compound naevi.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124786,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124787,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Naevus spilus is a benign neoplasm. Patients with larger or segmental manifestations of naevus spilus may be at increased risk of developing a melanoma {25072686; 21571187; 28293687}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:29:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]